@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
title Plain console: queued input and waiting updates

box "Background reader"
participant "inputThread:\nThread" as input
participant "reader:\nBufferedReader" as reader
end box
queue "inputQueue:\nBlockingQueue" as queue
box "Main thread"
participant "KeyboardWarrior" as main <<class>>
participant "machine:\nStateMachine" as machine
participant "current:\nState" as state
end box

note over input, state
  Scope: runPlainLoop(...) after setup.
  Only the main thread changes application states.
  Output and reader cleanup are omitted.
end note
par read complete lines
  loop until EOF, failure or interruption
    input -> reader : readLine()
    reader --> input : line
    input -> queue : offer(...)
    queue --> input
    note over input, queue
      Queued PlainInput wraps a line,
      EOF or IOException, in FIFO order.
    end note
  end
else dispatch and wait
  loop while running
    main -> queue : poll(...)
    queue --> main : next
    alt next contains a line
      main -> machine : handleInput(...)
      machine -> state : handleInput(...)
      state --> machine
      machine --> main
    else next marks EOF
      main -> machine : stop()
      machine --> main
      note over main, state : Leave the loop.
    else next contains a failure
      note over main, state
        Throw next.failure().
        Finally stop the state if still running.
      end note
    end
    opt still running
      main -> machine : updateWaiting()
      machine -> state : updateWaiting()
      state --> machine
      machine --> main
    end
  end
end
note over main, state
  Queue polling waits up to 100 ms.
  updateWaiting() can reveal a reaction command.
  Full update() and automatic typing submission stay disabled.
  Enter supplies the response and actual elapsed time.
end note
@enduml
